governance/audits/2026-08-21-toolchain/E-ledgers.md:56:- **`lumos code-loop check`** (tier=high gate) — **hard enforcement**, confirmed at `scripts/hooks/pre-push:99-118`: on push, if `pitfalls --diff` hits `tier: high`, the hook calls `lumos code-loop check` and **blocks the push (exit non-zero)** unless converged or explicitly `lumos code-loop skip --note "..."`. This is a real, mechanically-enforced gate, not honor-system. Evidence it fires: `governance/code-loop/main.json` shows a skip event from today; `docs/.governance-log.jsonl` has 79 `code-loop` events.
